/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-128687863,imgsize-34420.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India to Bangladesh: Want ties to be people-centric]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/128689083.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[India has conveyed its desire to strengthen people-centric cooperation with the new Bangladesh government, aiming for a positive and constructive bilateral relationship. This message was delivered by Indian High Commissioner Pranay Verma to the foreign minister and state minister, emphasizing mutual interest and benefit. Both nations have agreed to maintain regular engagement to further solidify their ties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/india-to-bangladesh-want-ties-to-be-people-centric/articleshow/128689083.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/india-to-bangladesh-want-ties-to-be-people-centric/articleshow/128689083.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-02-23T02:23:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ahsan Tasnim</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-128689133,imgsize-19478.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bid to undermine Dhaka's cooperation with Beijing doomed to failure: China]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/128687913.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[China affirmed its readiness to boost cooperation with Bangladesh's new government, warning that attempts to disrupt their partnership are destined to fail. This comes amid US concerns over Chinese influence in South Asia and a US emphasis on a free and open Indo-Pacific. Beijing also expressed hope for progress on the Teesta River project.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/bid-to-undermine-dhakas-cooperation-with-beijing-doomed-to-failure-china/articleshow/128687913.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/bid-to-undermine-dhakas-cooperation-with-beijing-doomed-to-failure-china/articleshow/128687913.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-02-23T01:11:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ahsan Tasnim</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-128688145,imgsize-20906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No thanks': Greenland, Denmark reject Trump's hospital ship offer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/128687891.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Denmark and its territory Greenland on Sunday rejected Donald Trump's offer to send a naval hospital ship to the Arctic island coveted by the US leader.  "President Trump's idea to send a US hospital ship here to Greenland has been duly noted.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/no-thanks-greenland-denmark-reject-trumps-hospital-ship-offer/articleshow/128687891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/no-thanks-greenland-denmark-reject-trumps-hospital-ship-offer/articleshow/128687891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-02-23T01:10:43+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-128688186,imgsize-80400.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Who killed Mexican drug lord El Mencho? Air Canada suspends operation in Puerto Vallarta; tourists asked to stay inside resorts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/128687485.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/who-killed-mexican-dru